#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:7
#: 52222939db0949d0950f23bd0cd9f940
msgid "Mission Rewind on Resume"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:9
#: 639d20c43d19460b96128c1c04fef1d2
msgid "This page explains what the mission rewind-on-resume feature is and how to use the feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:11
#: 9238d66a524b4cd1ade3f1990c4c2b9a
msgid "In certain applications or operating areas it can be common to interrupt a mission, for the purposes of deconfliction, by changing to another mode and manoeuvring the vehicle away from the planned mission path.  When ready to resume the mission, the normal behaviour of the vehicle is to fly/drive directly to the last 'active' waypoint that was loaded in the mission.  This behaviour is illustrated below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:20
#: 053fbd772ab94e0e8135233b3d410b35
msgid "As it can be seen, this leaves a significant portion of the planned mission that is either covered with incorrect track and heading or is not covered at all.  This becomes an issue for data gathering missions such as surveys, resulting in legs of the mission needing to be repeated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:24
#: 9aee94884af84c76a145101983daa050
msgid "The rewind-on-resume feature remedies this behaviour.  A rewind distance is defined by the operator.  When the mission is resumed the vehicle will return to the mission track at the desired distance behind the point that the mission was interrupted.  This gives the vehicle adequate time to achieve the desired track and heading before it achieves the position in which it was originally interrupted.  This behaviour can be seen below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:36
#: f9be10296d56488bbed4ef2e756171d2
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:38
#: f747829c057449c28ac8e233a8093ebc
msgid "The rewind-on-resume feature is enabled by setting a DO_SET_RESUME_REPEAT_DIST mission item.  This can be done in one of two ways:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:42
#: a46f3ee5b5b94b9ab217b3a822b634ab
msgid "**1) Ground control station recognises the DO_SET_RESUME_REPEAT_DIST mission item**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:44
#: 0386fcd386fd436992d2e355192c9273
msgid "Add a DO_SET_RESUME_REPEAT_DIST mission item from the point in the mission that you wish to enable the feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:45
#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:51
#: 89e59de3ef3d493ab368ab2786d3ef7a
#: 5b4add2fe2fa41a08cb583f29c3b4c55
msgid "Set the first data column to be the distance in meters that you want the mission to be rewound to, on resume."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:48
#: b90b7b938f194b378f9b840443669958
msgid "**2) Ground control station does not recognise the DO_SET_RESUME_REPEAT_DIST mission item**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:50
#: ca1aacd0230f400bafa54147e076e075
msgid "Add an UNKNOWN mission item from the point in the mission that you wish to enable the feature and set the MAVLink ID to 215."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:55
#: fa29597bd05e464a8e796fe986a1e212
msgid "The MIS_RESTART parameter must be set to zero, to prevent the mission restarting, for this feature to work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:57
#: 270fd688ff3e4837a879c0c0eaf916bd
msgid "To check that the rewind distance has been correctly set in the mission, monitor the message output in the ground control station.  When the vehicle registers the command the following message will be displayed: \"Resume repeat dist set to <DISTANCE> m\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:61
#: f8eca790d53a40e3976979f105de5a8f
msgid "Multiple DO_SET_RESUME_REPEAT_DIST commands can be set throughout the mission.  This provides the operator the ability to vary the rewind distance or switch the feature on/off throughout the mission, where extreme care and accuracy is required to manoeuvre the vehicle on certain mission legs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:65
#: 588edd0e8fe74d5097a7ef836e2ea593
msgid "This feature can be switched off by setting a DO_SET_RESUME_REPEAT_DIST mission item with a distance of zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:68
#: 62ca5fa4fa0d4e12ab42c5f3ee3437b4
msgid "When identifying the resume distance needed, a sensible value to try for most vehicles is twice the minimum turn radius.  The only exception is vehicles that can turn on the spot (multi-rotors and some rovers), in which a sensible distance would be twice the WP_RADIUS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:74
#: 5d16e9c267744682b8aa33d499f31e59
msgid "How it works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:76
#: aa95d19e4eb547afb03f155e9edc4386
msgid "Once enabled ArduPilot starts recording the waypoints that are successfully loaded as 'active'.  A history of up to seven waypoints are stored.  Upon a mission rewind-and-resume the mission history will be searched until either:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:79
#: b1bf0704e2994ffb99853d5a3179e61e
msgid "A position in the mission track is found that satisfies the rewind distance requirement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:80
#: fdf36b188fbf4846a4636e7beaf5fcb6
msgid "The end of stored mission history is found, in which case the resume position will be the last waypoint stored in the history."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:82
#: edde13c7a15a440bb532f9eebcde5c77
msgid "The vehicle will then resume to that location on the mission track and continue the mission as planned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:85
#: 8f1a9735dee8407983bb251e90d9669f
msgid "Height is accounted for in the resuming position.  If the vehicle is resuming to a location along the mission track whereby the aircraft is changing altitude, the height of the resuming position will be linearly interpolated between the two neighbouring waypoints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:90
#: 313f028549284c7980f745e34cdb7ec0
msgid "To prevent the vehicle from storing an obscure history and resuming to an unexpected location, if the mission is altered by using the set waypoint feature in a ground control station or a script, the history is reset.  This prevents the vehicle from rewinding the mission back past the point that the history was reset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:95
#: bdfa32e889cb47aeb3ec341c5c28a29d
msgid "This feature works with DO_JUMP commands and the jump count is not incremented whilst the vehicle is resuming the mission."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:98
#: ee202bec10db4e9fafeb0d6d24b9834d
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:100
#: d7e0ab1572fe414b9cdba3c61abc5ae5
msgid "**1) Short mission legs:** If the mission has closely spaced waypoints and the requested rewind distance is greater than the distance covered by the last six waypoints that have been passed, then the vehicle will resume on the 'oldest' waypoint stored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:104
#: 22e095fae58248b5a25e28d4dcdacc6e
msgid "**2) Spline waypoints:**  This feature will work with spline waypoints.  However, the accuracy of the resume distance will be diminished as the distance calculation is based on a straight line between navigation command locations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-rewind.rst:107
#: cdd434bfc7a44f30a24362f8b200bde8
msgid "**3) Non-waypoint navigation commands:**  This feature works with non-waypoint navigations commands, for example LOITER_TURNS. However, the distance calculation does not account for the distance of the vehicle track in those commands.  Using the previous example, the distance calculation does not account for the distance flown in the loiter."
msgstr ""
